course: dictionary
lesson: 5169
title: The word island
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An island is a piece of land with water all around it. Use the clues in the sentence to check: «Ireland is the green island to the west of Great Britain» tells you Ireland is land, and it sits in the sea near Britain.
explain: The word island can also mean anything that stands alone, surrounded by something different. A traffic island is a safe spot in the middle of a road where people can stop halfway across. A kitchen island is a block standing alone in the middle of the room.
explain: Stories use the idea too. A «desert island» or a castaway tells you the hero is alone and must survive. When you meet island in a new text, ask: is it land surrounded by water, or something standing alone? Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: An island is a piece of land with water all around it.
fact: A group of islands is called an archipelago.
fact: Great Britain and Ireland are islands, while Australia is so big it is called a continent.
fact: «Sicily is the biggest island in the Mediterranean Sea.»
fact: Islands can form from volcanoes or coral.
exercise: «Ireland is the green island to the west of Great Britain.» What is an island? | *A piece of land with water all around it | A kind of shark | A road with cars on both sides | A tall building in a city
exercise: A traffic island lets people do what? | Park their cars underground | *Stop halfway across the road | Fly over the road | Swim across the road
exercise: Which word means a group of islands? | volcano | *archipelago | continent | castaway
test: In a story, what does «a desert island» tell you about the hero? | The hero is in a busy city | *The hero is alone and must survive | The hero is going shopping | The hero is a famous king
test: «Hammerhead sharks ... gather in big schools near islands.» Where do the sharks gather? | On a traffic island in a road | In the middle of a desert | *Near islands, in the sea | Inside a volcano on land
exam: «Kiritimati, an island in Kiribati, is 14 hours ahead of London.» What is Kiritimati? | *An island in Kiribati | A city in London | A type of road | A famous shark
